{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The rider's own claim is that the trip ran 15.52 km against a quoted 11.2 km. The governing measurement under POL-RD-01 is gps_trace.trace_distance_km, which the trace records at 15.52 km, and the platform's optimal route estimate stored on the trip record is 11.2 km. The excess is therefore 4.32 km, or 38.57% of optimal. Both establishment tests pass: 4.32 km is greater than the 0.8 km absolute threshold and 38.57% is greater than the 20% percentage threshold. The deviation is established on this trip's own trace.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02803", "EV-TRIP-02803"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's explanation is that traffic was heavy so he took another road. That is an assertion of an external traffic cause, and under POL-RD-13 it is tested against the traffic_advisory for this trip and nothing else. The bundle holds no traffic_advisory covering this trip window: EV-ADVIS-02803-01 is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and no payload. The comparison POL-RD-03 requires cannot be run, POL-RD-03 is unavailable, and the driver's traffic assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08. The driver cites no advisory identifier, so this is a gap in the bundle rather than an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact, and the deviation stands at the measured figure.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02803-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-13", "POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "derived.advisory_area.advisories",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's assertion that traffic was heavy is unsupported by any traffic_advisory ID. Under POL-RD-08 the rider carries the initial burden and has discharged it with matching trip identifiers and a threshold-meeting excess on an unimpaired trace; the burden then shifts to the driver, who must point to a specific artifact and a specific clause to invoke POL-RD-03, POL-RD-04, POL-RD-05, POL-RD-11 or POL-RD-12. A general assertion that traffic was bad, unsupported by a traffic_advisory ID, does not discharge that burden. The driver has pointed to no artifact and no clause.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02803", "EV-GPS-02803", "EV-FARE-02803"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The GPS trace is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07. It carries 122 fixes at a 10 second sample interval with 100.0% coverage, zero gaps and a maximum gap of 0.0 seconds. None of limbs (a) to (c) fires: there is no gap over 90 seconds, no straight-line jump over 500 m, and no sustained sampling interval above 30 seconds. The trace is therefore fully usable to establish the deviation, and no independent corroboration under POL-RD-07(ii) is required.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02803"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07"],
      "relies_on": "max_gap_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No exculpatory clause on the driver's side is available on this record. There is no chat_log content at all: EV-CHAT-02803 carries 0 messages, so POL-RD-04 cannot be run and no rider-requested detour can be shown. The trip record shows no pickup or dropoff amendment: pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are both null and amended_optimal_distance_km is null, so POL-RD-05 does not apply. The vehicle type is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12 does not apply. The fare model is METERED, not UPFRONT_QUOTE, so POL-RD-11 does not apply. The excess stands unadjusted.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02803", "EV-TRIP-02803", "EV-FARE-02803"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-05", "POL-RD-12", "POL-RD-11"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.fare_model",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The refund is arithmetic under POL-RD-02. The fare model is METERED and the surge multiplier recorded on the fare breakdown is 1.5. The recomputed fare is ((3.80 + 0.75 x 11.2 + 0.28 x 15.1) x 1.5) + 0.80 platform fee + 2.00 ERP on the optimal route = (3.80 + 8.40 + 4.228) x 1.5 + 0.80 + 2.00 = 16.428 x 1.5 + 2.80 = 24.642 + 2.80 = 27.442. The charged total is 34.44. The refund is 34.44 - 27.442 = 6.998, rounded up to the nearest SGD 0.05, which is 7.00. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis and well below the 90% full-refund share, so the outcome is a partial refund of SGD 7.00.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02803", "EV-TRIP-02803"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.recomputed_fare",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The single ERP line on this fare, CTE Braddell southbound at SGD 2.00, is on the optimal route: the fare breakdown records on_optimal_route as true and the trace's nearest fix to the gantry is 7.52 m, well within the 250 m match radius. Under POL-RD-09(1) that charge is already comprehended in the POL-RD-02 recomputation, which includes only on-optimal-route gantries, and must not be added on top of the refund figure. The off-optimal-route ERP total is 0.00, so there is no standalone pass-through correction to make and no billing-integrity defect under POL-RD-09(4).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02803", "EV-GPS-02803"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.erp_lines",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The excess of 4.32 km is 38.57% of optimal, which is below the 50% and 8.0 km material-deviation thresholds in POL-RD-01, so this is not a MATERIAL deviation and the POL-RD-06 driver_profile check is not triggered. Even if it were consulted, the driver's deviation_flags_90d is 0 and completed_trips_90d is 413, so no pattern is established under POL-RD-06 and no FULL_REFUND uplift or conduct referral follows. The driver's lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter is context only under POL-GEN-01 and may not be substituted for the trailing-90-day figure.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-02803", "EV-GPS-02803"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's profile does not weaken the claim. rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 1, below the 4-or-more trigger in POL-RD-08, so no additional corroboration beyond the gps_trace is required for this claim. The rider's other profile fields are context only under POL-GEN-01 and are not relied on here.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-02803"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

