  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 7.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver, this is the decision on trip TRP-02803. The route actually driven is measured from the GPS trace (EV-GPS-02803) at 15.52 km between the recorded pickup and dropoff events, against the platform's booked optimal of 11.2 km on the trip record (EV-TRIP-02803). That is an excess of 4.32 km, or 38.6% of optimal. Both tests in POL-RD-01 are met (over 0.8 km and over 20%), so the deviation is established on this trip's own trace. The trace is clean for policy purposes: 122 fixes, a steady 10-second interval, 100% coverage, no gaps and a maximum gap of 0.0 seconds, so POL-RD-07(a)-(c) do not fire and no independent corroboration is required. DRIVER: your explanation that traffic was heavy is not accepted. No traffic advisory is on file for this trip - EV-ADVIS-02803-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT - and you named no advisory identifier. Under POL-RD-13 an uncited external-traffic assertion is tested against the advisory for the trip and nothing else; with no advisory the comparison cannot be run, POL-RD-03 is unavailable, and the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08. Because you cited no advisory, the absence is a gap in the bundle rather than the contradiction that sends a case to a human reviewer, so the case does not escalate on that ground. RIDER: your refund is arithmetic under POL-RD-02. The fare model is METERED and the surge multiplier of 1.5 is read from the fare breakdown (EV-FARE-02803): ((3.80 + 0.75 x 11.2 + 0.28 x 15.1) x 1.5) + 0.80 platform fee + 2.00 on-route ERP = 27.442. You were charged 34.44 (EV-FARE-02803). The difference is 6.998, rounded up to SGD 7.00. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis and at 20.3% of the charge it is far below the 90% full-refund level, so the outcome is a partial refund, not a full one. The SGD 2.00 CTE Braddell southbound ERP line is already comprehended in that figure under POL-RD-09(1) - it is itemised for transparency and is not added on top. It was matched to the trace 7.52 m from fix index 14, well inside the 250 m radius, so there is no phantom gantry, no billing-integrity defect and no referral on that ground. On driver conduct: the excess of 4.32 km is below both materiality lines (50% of optimal, and 8.0 km absolute), so this is not a MATERIAL deviation, and in any event the driver's trailing-90-day deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 413 completed trips, so no repeat-deviation pattern is established under POL-RD-06. No FULL_REFUND uplift and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral follow. The lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter mentioned in the debate is context only under POL-GEN-01 and was not used, and the rider-profile corroboration gate in POL-RD-08 is not engaged (deviation_claims_60d is 1, below 4). No POL-RD-10 escalation trigger fires: the identifiers match across trip record, trace and fare breakdown; the trace is unimpaired; the refund is far under SGD 150 and under the charge; and the only charge line (the ERP gantry) has a trace counterpart. The monetary effect of SGD 7.00 does not exceed the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so it is executed automatically. Two citation-stage claims that cited the missing advisory without disclosing its issue code were discarded by the referee and are recorded in the audit; the outcome does not turn on them."
  },
