    {
      "claim": "The driver's traffic excuse does not discharge the shifted burden. His counterparty statement says only 'Traffic was heavy so I took another road' - a general assertion with no traffic_advisory ID cited. POL-RD-08 is explicit that a general assertion that traffic was bad, unsupported by a traffic_advisory ID, does not discharge the driver's burden, and assertions that cite no evidence ID carry no weight.",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-02803-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "side": "RIDER"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The driver's explanation is that traffic was heavy so he took another road. That is an assertion of an external traffic cause, and under POL-RD-13 it is tested against the traffic_advisory for this trip and nothing else. The bundle holds no traffic_advisory covering this trip window: EV-ADVIS-02803-01 is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and no payload. The comparison POL-RD-03 requires cannot be run, POL-RD-03 is unavailable, and the driver's traffic assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08. The driver cites no advisory identifier, so this is a gap in the bundle rather than an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact, and the deviation stands at the measured figure.",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-02803-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "side": "DRIVER"
    }
  ]
}

