    "explanation": "Both of you, on trip TRP-02803. The platform's own GPS trace measures the route actually driven at 15.52 km; the platform's booking estimate for the shortest route was 11.2 km. The difference is 4.32 km, which is 38.57% over the estimate. Both tests in POL-RD-01 are crossed — more than 20% and more than 0.8 km — so the route deviation is established. I have used the trace figure (15.52 km), not the trip record's rounded 15.5 km, because POL-RD-01 says the trace governs.\n\nThe driver says traffic was heavy and he took another road. An external-traffic excuse can only be tested against a traffic advisory for this trip, and there is none in the bundle: EV-ADVIS-02803-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT. With no advisory on file the comparison cannot be run, POL-RD-03 is unavailable, and the excuse carries no weight (POL-RD-13, POL-RD-08); no distance is excused. The chat log is empty, so no rider-requested detour applies (POL-RD-04). The pickup and dropoff pins were never amended (POL-RD-05). The trip was not a pooled trip, and the fare was metered, not upfront, so neither POL-RD-12 nor POL-RD-11 applies.\n\nThe refund is arithmetic under POL-RD-02. Recomputed fare = ((3.80 + 0.75 x 11.2 + 0.28 x 15.1) x 1.5 surge) + 0.80 platform fee + 2.00 on-route ERP = 27.442. Charged total = 34.44. Refund = 34.44 - 27.442 = 6.998, rounded up to SGD 7.00. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor and far below the 90% full-refund share. The surge multiplier of 1.5 is read from the fare breakdown, not assumed absent. The single ERP line, CTE Braddell southbound SGD 2.00, is on the optimal route and is already included in the recomputed fare, so it is itemised for transparency but not added again (POL-RD-09(1)); there is no off-route ERP and no phantom gantry, so no billing-integrity finding arises.\n\nThe excess is below the 50% and 8.0 km materiality lines, so no POL-RD-06 pattern uplift or conduct referral arises; in any event the driver's trailing-90-day deviation count is 0 over 413 completed trips. The trace is clean — 122 fixes, 10-second sampling, no gaps — so no POL-RD-07 impairment and no POL-RD-10 escalation trigger fires. Both parties' profile fields other than the counters the clauses name (POL-GEN-01) were treated as context only and decided nothing.\n\nThe refund of SGD 7.00 does not exceed the SGD 8.00 automatic-execution threshold and will be executed automatically. This is a provisional ruling made without human review; either party may appeal it under POL-GEN-04."
  },
